  "$comment": [
    "Proposed Ukrainian patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.uk of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned.uk, seOwnedLead.uk, reserved.G1.uk). Not merged: the owner decides (M3 uk translator, 2026-10-06).",
    "Coverage: every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns and no uk key yet (25 rules, hype included: it has per-locale keys besides '*'). Skipped: selection-translate and jargon (already have uk), io-home and engine-claim ('*' only).",
    "Matching as in the validator: case-insensitive with the u flag, on the rendered text. In JavaScript \\b and \\w are ASCII-only even with the u flag, so these patterns use \\p{L} and (?<![\\p{L}]) / (?![\\p{L}]) as word boundaries; Ukrainian stems take any case ending through \\p{L}*. Apostrophes are written as [’'ʼ].",
    "Tested on the uk copy (0 hits outside the rules' exempt keys) and on the counter-examples listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/uk-qa.md, appendix A.",
    "seOwnedLead is applied to every H2 of every locale (validate-dist D-8); the uk pattern only matches a Ukrainian opening. It anchors with ^[\\s\\p{P}\\p{S}]* instead of ^\\W*: \\W also matches Cyrillic letters, so ^\\W* would let the phrase start anywhere in a Cyrillic H2."
  ],
